(During my stay in America I have had the privilege of addressing) Tj T*
(public audiences in every part, from New Orleans to Toronto, and) Tj T*
(from New York and Boston to San Francisco and Seattle; as well as) Tj T*
(more special audiences at Johns Hopkins University, at Saranac) Tj T*
(and at Harvard, California, Washington, and Yale Universities;) Tj T*
(and at the request of many friends some of the addresses given to) Tj T*
(these audiences are now published in volume form. These addresses) Tj T*
(briefly outline some of the lessons of long experience, and although) Tj T*
(the conditions under which they were delivered rendered complete) Tj T*
(exposition impracticable, there are, I think, advantages in not) Tj T*
(overloading the presentation for public consideration of a many-sided) Tj T*
(subject.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It will be noted that the same problem may be mentioned in several) Tj T*
(addresses, though usually from a different angle. The entire) Tj T*
(avoidance of repetition would have necessitated the abandonment of) Tj T*
(the lecture form, and would, I believe, have diminished the utility) Tj T*
(of the volume. The table of contents and index render cross-reference) Tj T*
(easy.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Those wishing to ascertain fuller details on most of the problems) Tj T*
(discussed in the present volume may refer, I think with advantage,) Tj T*
(to my annual reports as Medical Officer of the Local Government) Tj T*
(Board, England, and to my four special reports on Maternal and Child) Tj T*
(Mortality, which also were issued as English Government publications.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(British experience is only partially applicable in the United) Tj T*
(States, the almost complete Home Rule in each State creating a) Tj T*
(new and interesting problem in efficient national public health) Tj T*
(administration. Nevertheless a review of events in Great Britain) Tj T*
(cannot fail to be useful in America, which is faced with similar) Tj T*
(problems. The main lines of public health administration in Great) Tj T*
(Britain have proved their value by their success. There has been) Tj T*
(local independence with a minimum of central control, and the) Tj T*
(people?s representatives in every area have been made to realize) Tj T*
(their commercial responsibility. The mistakes made in permitting the) Tj T*
(multiplication of small and inefficient public health authorities,) Tj T*
(in allowing official medical work to be divided respectively) Tj T*
(between different local and central authorities, in sanctioning the) Tj T*
(creation of _ad hoc_ authorities for special work, in associating) Tj T*
(state medicine with monetary insurance against sickness, and in) Tj T*
(not securing that insurance shall directly assist the prevention) Tj T*
(of sickness, have been largely the mistakes of politicians and of) Tj T*
(central authorities. These mistakes involve the retracing of steps) Tj T*
(and the undoing of the mischief resulting from ill-advised action. In) Tj T*
(view of these conflicting events, the marvellous achievements secured) Tj T*
(by public health authorities are the more noteworthy.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In every American city visited by me I have been struck with the) Tj T*
(earnest desire of voluntary and official public health and social) Tj T*
