(                              CHAPTER I) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  PUBLIC HEALTH PROGRESS IN ENGLAND DURING THE LAST FIFTY YEARS[1]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(After thirty-five years in active public health work in) Tj T*
(England?during eleven of those years having been the principal) Tj T*
(officer of its central public health department on its medical) Tj T*
(side?I may be assumed to possess some qualification for the task) Tj T*
(of reviewing the past half century?s progress in public health in) Tj T*
(England.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(           _Parallelism of Events in New and Old England_) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(I find it, however, beyond my power to compass in a short address) Tj T*
(a resumé of my subject which shall be complete, or completely) Tj T*
(in perspective, or which shall not omit features on which,) Tj T*
(had time permitted, one would have wished to comment; and I) Tj T*
(must ask you to remember that only a portion?and that chiefly) Tj T*
(non-administrative[2]?of the history of this wonderful half century) Tj T*
(can be embraced within the present address. The survey should, I) Tj T*
(think, take a panoramic view of the story as it has developed, should) Tj T*
(note the changes as they have occurred, the obstacles which impeded) Tj T*
(reforms as well as the reforms secured; and should also, at least) Tj T*
(incidentally, state?in the light of unfailing historical guidance,) Tj T*
(as well as of increasing knowledge?the pressing desiderata for more) Tj T*
(efficient and more rapid future progress. I cannot hope to accomplish) Tj T*
(this task except to a fragmentary extent, but I am happy to remember) Tj T*
(that sanitary history in Old and in New England has proceeded largely) Tj T*
(on parallel lines. The curves of annual death-rates from all causes,) Tj T*
(from typhoid fever, from tuberculosis, and of the mortality of) Tj T*
(infants show the closeness of the parallelism of the public health) Tj T*
(history of England and Massachusetts.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The work of the last fifty years was built on preceding pioneer work) Tj T*
ET
