(of men in Old and in New England; and for a complete understanding of) Tj T*
(this work, a momentary glance is required at the men of this earlier) Tj T*
(generation and their work.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In the old country we speak with reverence of the names of Southwood) Tj T*
(Smith, Kay, Chadwick, Farr and Simon; and you remember with gratitude) Tj T*
(the names of Lemuel Shattuck, of Bowditch, of Walcott, S. W. Abbott,) Tj T*
(and Theobald Smith; and it is gratifying to remember that the) Tj T*
(epoch-making report of the Massachusetts Sanitary Commission of) Tj T*
(1850?to which were attached the ever memorable names of Shattuck,) Tj T*
(N. P. Banks, and Jehiel Abbott?among its many statesmanlike and) Tj T*
(far-seeing proposals, recommended a sanitary survey of the State, and) Tj T*
(referred to the recent English sanitary surveys, with which British) Tj T*
(sanitation may be said to have begun.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(                  _The Utilisation of Lay Workers_) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Let me in passing comment on the fact that neither Lemuel Shattuck in) Tj T*
(Boston nor Edwin Chadwick in London was a physician; but a perusal of) Tj T*
(their writings shows that they were men of sound judgment, of earnest) Tj T*
(zeal for their fellow men, with a wide and statesmanlike outlook,) Tj T*
(ready to search out, to accept and to apply the medical knowledge on) Tj T*
(which necessarily the prevention of disease is based. They illustrate) Tj T*
