(Historians in future generations will refer to the second half of the) Tj T*
(eighteenth and the first half of the nineteenth century as the period) Tj T*
(of unmitigated industrialism, of associated rapid increase of urban) Tj T*
(at the expense of rural life, and of the most extreme manifestation) Tj T*
(of _laissez faire_ economic science. The older semi-paternal system) Tj T*
(of interference with the economic life of the people by King and) Tj T*
(Parliament, was replaced, under the influence of Adam Smith,) Tj T*
(Malthus, James Mill, and other teachers, by inaction based on the) Tj T*
(view that in old countries poverty is the natural and inevitable) Tj T*
(result of pressure of population on means of subsistence, and that) Tj T*
(any interference with freedom of competition in obtaining work or) Tj T*
(employing workers is useless or mischievous. A similar view found) Tj T*
(expression in President Jefferson?s dictum: that government is best) Tj T*
(which governs least; and until the middle of the nineteenth century) Tj T*
(these views were generally accepted and their influence was dominant.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
