(paying exorbitant rents out of a miserable pittance of wages, and) Tj T*
(were exposed to the evils resulting from overcrowding, and from) Tj T*
(absence of adequate and satisfactory water supply, scavenging or) Tj T*
(drainage. By the year 1851 about half the population of England) Tj T*
(and Wales had become aggregated in towns; and it may be added that) Tj T*
(in 1911, less than one fourth of the population was left in rural) Tj T*
(districts. Urbanization in the earlier years meant dense overcrowding) Tj T*
(and insanitation; and that it is still an influence adverse to health) Tj T*
