() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Great War has changed our outlook on social, including medical,) Tj T*
(problems; and has made all of us consider anxiously in the midst of) Tj T*
(the terrible wreckage from war, what useful lessons may be garnered) Tj T*
(for our future guidance. In speaking of losses, I am not referring) Tj T*
(to financial burdens, though these are fabulously high?the bare) Tj T*
(statement that the British national debt has increased from 645 to) Tj T*
(near 8,000 millions sterling, brings this home?and we shall, most of) Tj T*
(us, go relatively poor for the rest of our lives and our children) Tj T*
(likewise. Nothing but the most effective and scientific use of our) Tj T*
(energies on the part of workers of every class can save us from) Tj T*
(protracted poverty.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
