(hearing and eyesight, and of reason, which have been experienced?one) Tj T*
(or other?in nearly every other family in the British Empire, and) Tj T*
(which show once more the wantonness of war: how cheaply life is held) Tj T*
(by it, how careless it is of the individual; and how disregardful it) Tj T*
(is of human promise and performance.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The destruction of over 700,000 lives of sharers in our common) Tj T*
(Empire, killed in battle or dead from wounds, represents an imperial) Tj T*
(loss, a terrible destruction of the real capital of the Empire?its) Tj T*
(manhood?and of the flower of that manhood; and generations will come) Tj T*
(and go before the Empire recovers completely.) Tj T*
