(of voluntary agencies, and will remain so, until local authorities) Tj T*
(\(which after all are manned by voluntary workers\) become saturated) Tj T*
(with the ideals of voluntary workers and of the new women-voters.) Tj T*
(Local authorities always have one great advantage over voluntary) Tj T*
(societies, that their action can be supported by legal powers.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The proper attitude of voluntary workers is to initiate and) Tj T*
(demonstrate the value of reforms, to persuade local authorities to) Tj T*
(adopt them, themselves to become members of these local authorities) Tj T*
(to ensure this end, and thus eventually render the voluntary) Tj T*
(organization for the object in question superfluous. There need be) Tj T*
(no fear; openings for further desirable voluntary work will always) Tj T*
(appear, as official work increases. In the main, however, the care) Tj T*
(of the health of the people is a governmental function, whether it) Tj T*
(has to do with the prevention of sickness or the satisfactory medical) Tj T*
(treatment and nursing of the sick.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(There is no early prospect of voluntary workers becoming unnecessary;) Tj T*
(for average human nature, as represented on governmental bodies, is) Tj T*
