(                             CHAPTER VII) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(         THE OBSTACLES TO AND IDEALS OF HEALTH PROGRESS[15]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(There are two ways in which Health Problems can be approached: what) Tj T*
(may be called the microscopic method, which examines in minute detail) Tj T*
(each individual problem; and the conspective method, in which an) Tj T*
(attempt is made to obtain an unbiased and comparative view of the) Tj T*
(chief problems concerned, in order that their relative importance may) Tj T*
(be assessed, and the possibilities of improvement may be gauged. In) Tj T*
(proposing to myself the latter and more difficult task, I appreciate) Tj T*
(the impossibility of discussing all the items which emerge.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(I would not have us forget what has already been achieved. Taking) Tj T*
(the national figures for England and Wales as an illustration, it) Tj T*
(is noteworthy that the death-rate from all causes fell from 22.4) Tj T*
(per 1,000 of population in 1846-50 to 13.8 in 1911-15, a reduction) Tj T*
(of nearly 40 per cent. Comparing the decennium 1871-80 with the) Tj T*
(quinquennium 1911-15, the incidence of reduction of death-rate at) Tj T*
(different ages was as follows:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(                _Percentage reduction in death-rate_) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(     Age) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(     0-5                42) Tj T*
(     5-10               48) Tj T*
(    10-15               43) Tj T*
(    15-20               46) Tj T*
(    20-25               51) Tj T*
(    25-35               50) Tj T*
(    35-45               42) Tj T*
(    45-55               25) Tj T*
(    55-65               15) Tj T*
(    65-75               10) Tj T*
(    75-85                7) Tj T*
(    85 and upwards      15) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The survey is saddened by the terrible losses of War, and the even) Tj T*
(more devastating ravages of influenza; and we realize our inadequacy) Tj T*
(to prevent catarrhal infections, until further research into) Tj T*
(preventive possibilities proves successful, and until the standard) Tj T*
(of universal conduct for catarrhal affections becomes much higher) Tj T*
(than at present. We realize furthermore that probably at least half) Tj T*
(the deaths from all causes which occur could be postponed until old) Tj T*
