(age. But the standard of health of the general population has greatly) Tj T*
(improved; typhus has practically disappeared under peace conditions;) Tj T*
(yellow fever approaches its demise; malaria and typhoid are) Tj T*
(controllable; tuberculosis and venereal diseases are only waiting for) Tj T*
(systematic, complete, and continuous measures to secure their rapid) Tj T*
(decline or actual disappearance; the mortality from childbearing and) Tj T*
(of young children has greatly declined; and this is an incomplete) Tj T*
(statement of what has already been done.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(                             _Obstacles_) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This improvement is all the more remarkable in view of the additional) Tj T*
(obstacles imposed to health improvement by modern conditions of urban) Tj T*
(and industrial life.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(                           _Urbanization_) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The population during the last century has steadily flocked to the) Tj T*
(towns from country districts. Streets have taken the place of green) Tj T*
(fields; rows of unsatisfactory dwellings have replaced country) Tj T*
(cottages; we have dust and belching smoke and noise instead of) Tj T*
(sunshine and country air and quiet; bustle and turmoil instead of) Tj T*
(life in close touch with mother-earth: and this change has been) Tj T*
(associated with an almost unlimited inter-communication of human) Tj T*
(beings, and a corresponding increase in opportunities for the) Tj T*
(convection of germs of disease.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Until the time of the industrial revolution in England modes of) Tj T*
(locomotion were little if any more advanced than among the ancient) Tj T*
(Egyptians; and disease, when it travelled at all, travelled by slow) Tj T*
(and deliberate stages. Now the infections of the entire world may be) Tj T*
(sampled in any one district in the course of a few weeks. Man has, in) Tj T*
(fact, reverted from the land-tied condition involved in agriculture) Tj T*
(to the migratory habits of an earlier period of man?s life on the) Tj T*
(earth. As Wells has put it: ?in every locality ... countless people) Tj T*
(are delocalised,? and it is not the least evil of urbanization that,) Tj T*
(in consequence of this, the administration of local affairs falls) Tj T*
