(My task is to attempt to give a bird?s-eye view of ?The Methods of) Tj T*
(Controlling Tuberculosis in England,? and to revaluate, as far as) Tj T*
(is practicable, in the light of many years? study of the disease,) Tj T*
(the relative value of the measures which historically have been) Tj T*
(followed by the greatly reduced mortality from tuberculosis. The) Tj T*
(subject teems with difficulties, and as you are aware there is no) Tj T*
(unanimity of opinion when tuberculosis is thus considered. This is) Tj T*
(the more surprising in view of our present accurate knowledge of the) Tj T*
(pathology of disease caused by bovine and human tubercle bacilli, and) Tj T*
(in view of the fairly general unanimity of opinion as to the methods) Tj T*
(of control which are needed to secure still more rapid reduction) Tj T*
(of the devastations of tuberculosis. This general opinion may, I) Tj T*
(think, be summarised in the statement which I have made elsewhere,) Tj T*
(that the removal or diminution of infection from each single case of) Tj T*
(tuberculosis reduces correspondingly the prospect of further cases,) Tj T*
(but that tuberculosis will not be completely controlled until every) Tj T*
(tuberculous patient receives such care throughout the whole course of) Tj T*
(his life, as will ensure his welfare and will obviate the likelihood) Tj T*
(of his infecting others.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
