(                  _Basic Facts as to Tuberculosis_) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Tuberculosis is a chronic infectious disease with a low degree of) Tj T*
(infectivity. Circumstances favouring infection have a high degree of) Tj T*
(importance; but tuberculosis does not develop in the absence of the) Tj T*
(tubercle bacillus. No infection, no disease.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. Tuberculosis may remain latent in the system for many years, and) Tj T*
(there is strong reason for thinking that the infection of a large) Tj T*
(proportion of early adult tuberculosis was acquired in childhood.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. The two types of tubercle bacilli, bovine and human, are) Tj T*
(stable both in character and in degree of virulence, and are not) Tj T*
(interchangeable so far as can be shown by protracted experimentation.) Tj T*
(The human type of bacillus is the chief source of infection of) Tj T*
(mankind, though bovine infection is not negligible.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Out of 98 children between the age of 2 and 10 years who had died in) Tj T*
(various hospitals from all causes unselected, 18 or 18.4 per cent.) Tj T*
(were found to have been infected by tubercle bacilli of the bovine) Tj T*
(type, and 81 or 81.6 per cent. by tubercle bacilli of the human) Tj T*
(type. \(Report on Investigations made in the Laboratory of the Local) Tj T*
(Government Board, Annual Report of the Medical Officer of the Local) Tj T*
(Government Board, 1913-14, p. lix.\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. Animal experimentation shows that in animals of the same) Tj T*
(species the extent of tuberculosis produced depends to a large and) Tj T*
(probably to a dominant extent on the number of tubercle bacilli) Tj T*
(introduced into the system. Although doubtless there are variations) Tj T*
(in susceptibility in families, and in each individual at different) Tj T*
(periods, there is little doubt that in the main the same rule holds) Tj T*
(good for mankind.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5. Experience shows that dusty occupations, indoor occupations,) Tj T*
(alcoholism, over-fatigue, an attack of acute illness, especially of) Tj T*
(influenza, measles, or enteric fever, increase the danger of minimal) Tj T*
(doses of tubercle bacilli, and serve to bring latent foci of disease) Tj T*
(into activity.) Tj T*
