(Hence notification of cases of tuberculosis was advocated for many) Tj T*
(years by pioneer medical officers of health who secured voluntary) Tj T*
(notification by doctors of a considerable proportion of the total) Tj T*
(cases in their districts, and in a few instances secured compulsory) Tj T*
(notification by local enactment, before any general regulations on) Tj T*
(the subject were made. It is noteworthy that in this early period a) Tj T*
(town like Brighton, which had voluntary notification with sanatorium) Tj T*
(provision for patients willing thus to be treated, secured the) Tj T*
(notification of a larger proportion of total cases than another town) Tj T*
(in which notification was compulsory, but no sanatorium accommodation) Tj T*
(had been provided. The point is mentioned as emphasizing the general) Tj T*
(principle that compulsory measures in public health, if they are to) Tj T*
(be successful, require to be associated with full provision for the) Tj T*
(action which should follow the compulsory enactment; which provision,) Tj T*
