(as in this case, may be a direct inducement to compliance with the) Tj T*
(enactment. In view of the change of central policy involved and of) Tj T*
(the unpreparedness of most local authorities to give the assistance) Tj T*
(needed for notified cases, the general enforcement of notification) Tj T*
(of tuberculosis was brought about in stages; in 1909 poor-law cases) Tj T*
(of consumption were made notifiable throughout England and Wales,) Tj T*
(hospital cases in 1911, consumption in the general community in 1912,) Tj T*
(and all forms of tuberculosis in 1913.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It was not anticipated that complete notification of cases would) Tj T*
(be obtained for some years, but a review of English national) Tj T*
(experience of notification of tuberculosis up to the present time) Tj T*
(necessitates the confession that there has been failure to secure) Tj T*
(the coöperation of an unexpectedly large proportion of the medical) Tj T*
(profession in this public-health duty. Many cases have never been) Tj T*
(notified and in a large number of other cases notification has been) Tj T*
(belated; Dr. Barwise, County Medical Officer of Health of Derbyshire,) Tj T*
(obtained information as to 417 deaths certified during 1917 to be) Tj T*
(due to tuberculosis, and found that of this number 39 per cent. had) Tj T*
(never been notified, and that over 70 per cent. had either not been) Tj T*
(notified or died within twelve weeks of notification. This may be an) Tj T*
(exceptionally bad experience; but the duty of notification in many) Tj T*
(areas is only imperfectly performed, and no adequate steps are being) Tj T*
(taken to diminish this default.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(As notification is the first step towards coördinated measures for) Tj T*
(the patient and in the interest of the public health, the causes) Tj T*
(of delay in notification and of failure to notify deserve further) Tj T*
(examination.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(                 _Causes of Failure in Notification_) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. The patient himself commonly is responsible for much delay in) Tj T*
(the recognition of his disease. A large proportion of consumptive) Tj T*
(patients refrain from applying for treatment until disease is) Tj T*
(fully established, and until they are incapacitated for work.) Tj T*
(Not infrequently this means that the patient does not consult a) Tj T*
(doctor until a few months or even weeks before his death. Until the) Tj T*
(conditions of general medical practice are altered, and every person) Tj T*
(has the right to state-paid medical consultations, belated recourse) Tj T*
(to medical advice will continue.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(With this there is badly needed further education of the public as to) Tj T*
(seeking advice for protracted colds and coughs, or for other symptoms) Tj T*
(suggestive of tuberculosis; and a wider hygienic propaganda as to) Tj T*
(housing, overcrowding, dusty indoor occupations, expectoration, etc.,) Tj T*
(is also called for.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. Under present conditions of medical practice, early diagnosis) Tj T*
(of tuberculosis often fails to be secured, even when the patient) Tj T*
(places himself under medical care. It is to the private practitioner) Tj T*
