(                      _Examination of Contacts_) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This branch of tuberculosis work is most important. Often the first) Tj T*
(notified case is not the first clinical case of tuberculosis in a) Tj T*
(given family; and from the standpoint of prevention the detection of) Tj T*
(such cases of longer standing is important. Examination of contacts) Tj T*
(also frequently discovers patients in an earlier and more curable) Tj T*
(stage of disease than the notified patient.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It is important that all home contacts of each notified case of) Tj T*
(tuberculosis should be examined; and one of the most important) Tj T*
(functions of the tuberculosis officer is to arrange for this. The) Tj T*
(examination may be carried out by arrangement at the tuberculosis) Tj T*
(dispensary; but otherwise, at the home of the invaded family. When) Tj T*
(there is a medical practitioner in attendance his coöperation and) Tj T*
(presence should as a rule be invited.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Such systematic examination of the household not only is more) Tj T*
(efficient in discovering sources of continuing infection than the) Tj T*
(desultory examination of a few contacts,?which often still represents) Tj T*
(the extent of this important work,?but it has in addition a greater) Tj T*
(educational effect on the public; and general recourse to such) Tj T*
(systematic observations would rapidly improve the prospect of) Tj T*
(satisfactory control of tuberculosis.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Even when examination of contacts is practised after notification) Tj T*
(of a case of pulmonary tuberculosis, it is too often neglected) Tj T*
(after notification of non-pulmonary cases. This represents a) Tj T*
(great public-health loss; the majority of cases of non-pulmonary) Tj T*
