(                   _Educational Work of Sanatoria_) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Apart from the question of cure, which with belated treatment can) Tj T*
(only be expected in a minority of cases, the sanatorium serves an) Tj T*
(important purpose, not only in restoring patients to a considerable) Tj T*
(degree of health and working capacity for a longer or shorter) Tj T*
(time, but also in educating the patients how to live and conduct) Tj T*
(themselves. A stay in a sanatorium for a short period?a month or) Tj T*
(six weeks?under doctors and nurses who realise the value of this) Tj T*
(work?would there were more of these!?secures the training of the) Tj T*
(patient on lines beneficial to his future health and enables him to) Tj T*
(obviate all danger for others.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In such a short stay in a sanatorium what may be called tuberculosis) Tj T*
(discipline can be and is acquired when the sanatorium is) Tj T*
(satisfactorily administered; and the patient thus disciplined is in) Tj T*
(a much more favorable position for securing his own welfare and that) Tj T*
(of others than the undisciplined patient, just as the soldier who has) Tj T*
(had routine drill under a competent instructor is more efficient) Tj T*
(than the untrained recruit.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
