() Tj T*
(                      _The Midwives Act, 1902_) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This Act forbade any woman after April 1, 1906, who was not certified) Tj T*
(under the Act, from using the title of midwife or any similar) Tj T*
(description of herself. It forbade after April 1, 1910, any such) Tj T*
(woman from ?habitually and for gain attending women in childbirth,) Tj T*
(except under the direction of a qualified medical practitioner?; and) Tj T*
(it forbade any certified midwife to use an uncertified person as her) Tj T*
(substitute. The Act defined the limits of function of the midwife) Tj T*
(by stating that the Act did not confer upon her any title to give) Tj T*
(certificates of death or of still-birth, or to take charge of any) Tj T*
(abnormality or disease in connection with parturition.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Act set up the Central Midwives Board, giving it special) Tj T*
(disciplinary powers over midwives. It also imposed on county councils) Tj T*
(and the councils of county boroughs the duty of supervising the work) Tj T*
(of midwives. For further details the Act itself and the Rules of the) Tj T*
(Central Midwives Board made under the Act should be consulted.) Tj T*
