(In many instances maternity nursing is required. The midwife may have) Tj T*
(too many patients to be able to give this during the ten days in) Tj T*
(which she is in charge of the patient; and even when she carries out) Tj T*
(her duty in this respect in accordance with the Rules of the Central) Tj T*
(Midwives Board additional help is required in the feeding and care of) Tj T*
(the mother and infant, and in the care of the household. Often also) Tj T*
(nursing is required for both mother and infant for a considerable) Tj T*
(period beyond the ten days. For these persons the government gives) Tj T*
(grants for maternity nursing and for ?home helps.?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Even when all the above requirements are or can be fulfilled, there) Tj T*
(remain a large number of cases of pregnant women, and especially) Tj T*
(of unmarried women, who cannot be satisfactorily confined at home,) Tj T*
(either because of their social or sanitary circumstances, or) Tj T*
(because abnormal or complicated childbirth is expected. For such) Tj T*
(cases hospital provision is needed. This is one of the most urgent) Tj T*
(requirements of the present time.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Under present conditions, institutional lying-in provision is) Tj T*
(chiefly voluntary in character; and the government has advised) Tj T*
(local authorities to contract for its use, rather than wait for the) Tj T*
(erection of special hospitals. In other instances houses are being) Tj T*
(taken and adapted as maternity homes.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(                          _Ante-natal Work_) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The progress made in the organisation of ante-natal work is slow for) Tj T*
(reasons which are fairly obvious. There has been difficulty under war) Tj T*
(conditions in securing assistance from doctors and midwives. There) Tj T*
(is the well-known difficulty as to notification of pregnancy, which) Tj T*
(the government has not encouraged, except when the definite consent) Tj T*
(of the mother has been previously obtained. The facilities for) Tj T*
(help provided at the Centre have in some areas attracted patients;) Tj T*
(and health visitors and midwives have done much in other areas to) Tj T*
(persuade mothers of the advisability of safeguarding themselves) Tj T*
(against possible complications, as well as of securing adequate) Tj T*
(preparation for the lying-in period.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This subject is closely associated with that of abortions,) Tj T*
(still-births, and deaths in the first two weeks after birth. One of) Tj T*
(the most promising methods for securing the sound development of) Tj T*
(ante-natal work consists in the investigation of still-births and) Tj T*
(early infant mortality. When these inquiries are made mothers can) Tj T*
(be induced to obtain medical advice not only at the time, but also) Tj T*
(in the event of a subsequent pregnancy. The investigation at the) Tj T*
(patient?s home of all such cases and assistance in prevention of) Tj T*
