(recurrence of unnecessary ante-natal, natal, and early post-natal) Tj T*
(deaths have as great an importance as the building up of a successful) Tj T*
(ante-natal clinic. The anti-syphilis work now being carried on will) Tj T*
(help greatly in this direction.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(                         _Dental Assistance_) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(There has been a large extension of dental assistance at Centres for) Tj T*
(expectant and for nursing mothers, and for children, especially in) Tj T*
(the metropolis and its vicinity. The government has lately extended) Tj T*
(its grant to cover dentures for mothers who are nursing or pregnant,) Tj T*
(if the medical officer of the Centre is satisfied that the woman?s) Tj T*
(health will be materially improved by the denture, and that she is) Tj T*
(unable to provide it for herself.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(                              _Creches_) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Creches and day nurseries may be expected to exercise influence in) Tj T*
(educating mothers in the care of their children. For this purpose it) Tj T*
(is very desirable to have the creche attached to or near an infant) Tj T*
(welfare centre.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(These creches, unless managed with the most rigid medical and) Tj T*
(general cleanliness, are very apt to spread infectious diseases; not) Tj T*
(merely such diseases as whooping cough, measles, and chickenpox,) Tj T*
(but also catarrhal and diarrh?al diseases. In the prevention of all) Tj T*
(of these the enforcement of the strictest cleanliness is essential,) Tj T*
(especially during the summer months for the last named diseases. For) Tj T*
(the prevention of catarrhal infections, it is essential that the) Tj T*
(creche should be conducted, so far as practicable, on strict open-air) Tj T*
(lines. Open-air creches give admirable occasional relief to mothers,) Tj T*
(even when these do not go out to work. The ?toddler?s playground?) Tj T*
(is a blessing to all concerned, but the indoor creche may be, and) Tj T*
(often is, mischievous. The risks are greatly reduced by insisting on) Tj T*
(open-air conditions and by not allowing large groups of children to) Tj T*
(come together. Smaller groups mean greatly decreased possibility of) Tj T*
(cross-infection.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(             _Observation Beds at Child Welfare Centres_) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(At infant welfare centres infants are not infrequently seen who) Tj T*
(fail to make progress while living at home, and who yet are not ill) Tj T*
(enough to be sent to a hospital. This especially applies to cases of) Tj T*
(defective nutrition. For these cases beds in connection with centres) Tj T*
(have been found to be necessary for observation purposes and to) Tj T*
(initiate further treatment. In some instances, especially for failure) Tj T*
(of breast-feeding, it is advisable to admit the mother with the) Tj T*
(infant.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
