(national asset which consists in a healthy population. During this) Tj T*
(period there was a great increase in the industrial employment of) Tj T*
(women, including married women, in factories including munition and) Tj T*
(other works. This increase it is believed amounted to a million and a) Tj T*
(half workers.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Notwithstanding the many adverse influences, to which must be added) Tj T*
(great overcrowding in many industrial areas, especially those in) Tj T*
(which new industries were hurriedly started, and the increasing cost) Tj T*
(of food and especially of milk with a scarcity of supply, it has been) Tj T*
(seen that infant mortality remained low and on the whole declined) Tj T*
(during the whole period of the war.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(To what circumstances can this be ascribed?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It is unnecessary to assume that this result was entirely due to the) Tj T*
(active measures favorable to maternity and child welfare which were) Tj T*
(taken as an unexampled scale, though these measures can claim an) Tj T*
(important share in the result.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A number of contributory factors were at work:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. In none of the years in question did the summer weather favor an) Tj T*
(excess of diarrh?al mortality. With this factor, however, eliminated) Tj T*
(the infant mortality each year was lower than in previous years.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. Although so many husbands were away from home, in a large) Tj T*
(proportion of cases the wife, in virtue of her separation allowance,) Tj T*
(was financially in a more favorable position than when she was) Tj T*
(dependent on her husband?s wages or such portion of it as he allowed) Tj T*
(her for the support of the household.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. In addition, every soldier became an insured person, and his wife) Tj T*
(was therefore entitled to the Maternity Benefit of 30 shillings on) Tj T*
(the birth of a child, and an additional 30 shillings if she was) Tj T*
(herself an employed person.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. There can be no reasonable doubt that the restrictions on the) Tj T*
(consumption of alcoholic drinks and the limitation of hours for) Tj T*
(opening public houses were a factor in improving domestic welfare.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(But attaching full value to these and other similar factors which) Tj T*
(undoubtedly were at work, chief place must, I think, be given to) Tj T*
(the awakening of the public conscience on the subject, and to the) Tj T*
(concentration on the mother and her child which had been urged in) Tj T*
(season and which now became a fact. An indication of the public) Tj T*
(mind is given by the advice issued by the Local Government Board in) Tj T*
(August, 1918, which is quoted on page 248.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
